{"id": "P08334", "name": "Mahaveer Prasad Taparia", "name_chinese": "玛哈维尔·普拉萨德·塔帕里亚", "country": "India", "net_worth_usd_m": "964.0", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time (former)", "source_of_wealth": "Plastics", "industry": "manufacturing", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (former) (2025); Forbes annual (2024); Hurun Global (2024-2025); Hurun India (2018-2019)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/mahaveer-prasad-taparia/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Mahaveer Prasad Taparia is the managing director of Mumbai-based plastics producer Supreme Industries.", "Supreme is one of India's largest plastic processors, making everything from moulded furniture to composite gas cylinders.", "The Mumbai-headquartered company also makes bathroom fittings and storage products in its 28 factories across India.", "His older brother Bajranglal Taparia, the company's chairman, and his nephew Shivratan Taparia Supreme's executive director, also have stakes in the company.", "Taparia also has a small stake in Supreme Petrochem, which produces polystyrene, used for construction and packaging."], "forbes_facts": []}
{"id": "P08451", "name": "Kate Wang", "name_chinese": "", "country": "China", "net_worth_usd_m": "923.0", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time (former)", "source_of_wealth": "e-cigarettes", "industry": "manufacturing", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (former) (2022); Forbes annual (2021)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/kate-wang/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Kate Wang is the CEO and cofounder of Chinese vaping company RLX Technology, which listed on the New York Stock Exchange in January 2021.", "RLX is the largest e-cigarette maker in China with nearly two thirds of the market, and Wang owns 20% of the company's shares.", "She cofounded the firm in early 2018 when she was still working at ride-hailing app Didi Chuxing and trying to get her father to quit smoking.", "Before joining Didi, Wang worked as a consultant at Bain & Co. and as a management trainee at consumer goods giant Procter & Gamble.", "RLX's sales grew rapidly from $20 million in 2018, its first year of operation, to $585 million in 2020."], "forbes_facts": ["RLX offers a range of flavors including mung bean-popsicle-flavored 'Ludou Ice,' designed to evoke nostalgia among older users who used to eat the popsicles as kids.", "One of Wang's favorite books is 'The Art of Loving' by German philosopher Erich Fromm, which she read while attending college in her home city of Xi'an."]}
